From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:51:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer eac3/ac3 over aac when transcoding multichannel audio

ShiftAudioCodecsIfNeeded only demoted dts/truehd for 6+ channel input, so
a client listing "aac,ac3,eac3,mp3" (Jellyfin Android TV 0.20.0-hero.31)
got AAC 5.1 for every TrueHD 7.1 source. Android TV decodes AAC to PCM,
and the Sony KD-65X75WL's app-facing PCM output is stereo-only, so the
soundbar received stereo. Native E-AC3 on the same TV is bitstreamed
(AudioTrack enc=eac3, 5.1).

For 6+ channel input, move eac3 then ac3 to the front when the client
lists them. Channel and bitrate caps for both already exist (6 ch,
640 kbps), so 7.1 sources become 5.1 E-AC3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs              | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MediaBrowser.Controller/MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs b/MediaBrowser.Controller/MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs
index 6f010c0242..aef51a8070 100644
--- a/MediaBrowser.Controller/MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs
+++ b/MediaBrowser.Controller/MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs
@@ -7601,6 +7601,22 @@ namespace MediaBrowser.Controller.MediaEncoding
                 audioCodecs.RemoveAt(0);
                 audioCodecs.Add(removed);
             }
+
+            if (inputChannels >= 6)
+            {
+                // A client that lists eac3/ac3 can bitstream them to an AV receiver, while multichannel aac has to be
+                // decoded to PCM on the client, which many TV apps can only output as stereo. Keep surround: prefer them.
+                foreach (var codec in new[] { "ac3", "eac3" })
+                {
+                    var index = audioCodecs.FindIndex(i => string.Equals(i, codec, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
+                    if (index > 0)
+                    {
+                        var preferred = audioCodecs[index];
+                        audioCodecs.RemoveAt(index);
+                        audioCodecs.Insert(0, preferred);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
         }
 
         private void ShiftVideoCodecsIfNeeded(List<string> videoCodecs, EncodingOptions encodingOptions)
